---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import TopologyScene from '../components/TopologyScene.astro';
import release from '../data/release.json';

const capabilities = [
  ['Native Wayland terminal', 'Included'],
  ['Persistent sessions', 'Included'],
  ['Panes, tabs, and restore', 'Included'],
  ['Automation with permissions', 'Optional'],
  ['Versioned releases', 'Available'],
  ['AUR package', release.packageVersion],
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Splinterm — a terminal you can come back to"
  preloadDisplayFont
  description="A terminal for Omarchy with panes, tabs, and work you can come back to. By default, shells keep running when you close the window."
>
  <section class="intro-hero" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <img class="intro-mark" src="/logo-transparent.png" alt="" width="768" height="768" />
    <h1 id="intro-title" class="intro-wordmark">splinterm</h1>
    <p class="intro-status">Splinterm {release.version} · Arch / Omarchy · x86_64</p>
    <p class="intro-thesis">A terminal for Omarchy with work you can come back to.</p>
    <div class="intro-actions" aria-label="Get started with Splinterm">
      <a class="button primary intro-primary" href="/docs/install/">Install Splinterm <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="#workflow">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="intro-install" aria-label="Recommended installation command">
      <span>Recommended</span>
      <code><i aria-hidden="true">$</i> yay -S splinterm-bin</code>
      <a href="/docs/status/">Release and limits</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="product" class="hero shell-section" aria-labelledby="product-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span>{release.channel} {release.version}</span> · Enter the Lair</p>
      <h2 id="product-title">Your shell should outlive its <em>window.</em></h2>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        By default, your shells keep running when you close the window. Open your Dojo again
        and pick up where you left off, with your panes and running commands still there.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/docs/install/">Install Splinterm <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="#workflow">Try it for yourself</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">The background service must stay running. You can also choose work that ends when its window closes. <a href="/docs/sessions/">See what stays running.</a></p>
    </div>
    <TopologyScene />
  </section>

  <section class="manifesto shell-section" aria-labelledby="persistence-title">
    <div class="section-index" aria-hidden="true">01 / Your workspace</div>
    <div class="manifesto-copy">
      <h2 id="persistence-title">Make room<br />for your work.</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>Lair</strong> holds your workspace. A <strong>Dojo</strong> is a layout shown in a tab.
        Each terminal pane is a <strong>Splint</strong>. Keep an editor beside your tests, or give your
        services their own Dojo.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/docs/presets/">Start with a ready-made layout</a> or arrange your own.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="sequence" aria-label="Persistent session workflow">
      <li><span>01</span><strong>Open</strong><small>Start a terminal from the desktop launcher.</small></li>
      <li><span>02</span><strong>Split</strong><small>Add panes for the things you’re working on.</small></li>
      <li><span>03</span><strong>Close</strong><small>Leave persistent work running in the background.</small></li>
      <li><span>04</span><strong>Return</strong><small>Choose your layout from Recent Dojos.</small></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="workflow" class="first-workflow shell-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Try it</p>
      <h2 id="workflow-title">Leave the window.<br />Return to the Dojo.</h2>
      <p>Open a terminal and press Ctrl+Shift+Enter to add a pane. With the default settings, you can close the window and use Recent Dojos to return to the same running work.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Follow the quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="button workflow-secondary" href="/docs/configure/configuration/#keymaps-and-the-command-palette">Coming from tmux?</a>
      </div>
      <p>Changed the lifetime settings? <a href="/docs/sessions/">Check what closing a window does</a> before trying this.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="command-stack" aria-label="Example Splinterm commands">
      <div><span>$</span><code>yay -S splinterm-bin</code><small>install</small></div>
      <div><span>$</span><code>splinterm-xdg-terminal-exec</code><small>open a terminal</small></div>
      <div><span>$</span><code>splinterm dojos</code><small>choose running work</small></div>
      <div><span>$</span><code>splinterm reopen</code><small>return to the last Dojo</small></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wayland-section shell-section" aria-labelledby="wayland-title">
    <div class="section-index" aria-hidden="true">02 / On your desktop</div>
    <div class="wayland-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Native Wayland</p>
      <h2 id="wayland-title">Built for Omarchy.</h2>
      <p>Splinterm works directly with Wayland for keyboard input, display scaling, and the clipboard—without XWayland in between.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/wayland/">How Wayland support works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="wayland-benefits">
      <article><span>Displays</span><h3>Use your display scale</h3><p>Follows the scale set for each output, including fractional scaling.</p></article>
      <article><span>Input</span><h3>Type your way</h3><p>Keyboard, mouse, copy and paste, compose keys, and input methods.</p></article>
      <article><span>Drawing</span><h3>Redraw what changed</h3><p>Updates changed areas rather than redrawing the whole window every time.</p></article>
      <article><span>Appearance</span><h3>Match your theme</h3><p>Follows Omarchy’s colors and, unless you set a font override, its monospace font family.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="wayland-boundary">Tested on x86_64 Omarchy/Arch with Hyprland. Other Linux desktops are not yet supported. Rendering uses the CPU, not the GPU.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="automation" class="control-section shell-section" aria-labelledby="control-title">
    <div class="section-index" aria-hidden="true">03 / Optional automation</div>
    <div id="automation-title" class="control-heading">
      <h2 id="control-title">A little help.<br />On your terms.</h2>
      <p>Connect scripts or an MCP tool to your workspace. They need permission before they can read output, type commands, or change your layout.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="control-grid">
      <article class="control-card human-card">
        <div class="card-label"><span>Tools</span><i>with permission</i></div>
        <h3>Help with the routine</h3>
        <p>Give a tool access to the work it needs, locally or over SSH.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Read output and search scrollback</li>
          <li>Create panes and run commands</li>
          <li>Follow changes as they happen</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="control-card automation-card">
        <div class="card-label"><span>Permissions</span><i>set by you</i></div>
        <h3>Choose what it can do</h3>
        <p>Permissions apply to a specific program, not every tool on your machine.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Limit which sessions it can access</li>
          <li>Choose which actions it can take</li>
          <li>Set time and output limits</li>
          <li>Revoke access when you’re done</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="boundary-note">
      <p><span aria-hidden="true">◆</span> Text printed in a terminal does not grant a tool permission to act.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/docs/automation/">Learn about tool permissions</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/mcp/">Set up MCP <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="status-section shell-section" aria-labelledby="status-title">
    <div class="section-index" aria-hidden="true">04 / Available now</div>
    <div class="status-intro">
      <h2 id="status-title">Available<br />for Omarchy.</h2>
      <p>Splinterm {release.version} is the first stable release for x86_64 Omarchy/Arch with Hyprland. It is not a long-term-support release or a 1.0 compatibility promise; future 0.x releases may need migration steps.</p>
      <p>Save your work before upgrading. Version 0.1 cannot keep commands running through a restart of its background service.</p>
      <div class="status-actions">
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/status/">What’s supported <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/packaging/">Upgrade safely <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-list">
      {capabilities.map(([name, status], index) => (
        <div class="capability-row">
          <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <strong>{name}</strong>
          <i>{status}</i>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-gateway shell-section" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Need a hand?</p>
      <h2 id="docs-title">Find what you need.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="gateway-links">
      <a href="/docs/quickstart/"><span>Get started</span><small>Install, open, split, and return.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/configure/configuration/"><span>Make it yours</span><small>Fonts, colors, keyboard shortcuts, and tmux-style controls.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/presets/"><span>Try a Dojo preset</span><small>Set up a complete layout in one go.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/sessions/"><span>Keep work running</span><small>What closes, what stays, and how to return.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/remote/"><span>Work over SSH</span><small>Open a Dojo on another machine.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/wayland/"><span>Understand Wayland support</span><small>How Splinterm works with your desktop.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/automation/"><span>Connect a tool</span><small>Choose its permissions and limits.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/mcp/"><span>Set up MCP</span><small>Install, connect, and authorize the adapter.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/roadmap/"><span>See what’s next</span><small>What we’re working on and what’s still an idea.</small><i>↗</i></a>
      <a href="/docs/development/"><span>Help build Splinterm</span><small>Source code, tests, and contributor guidance.</small><i>↗</i></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
